51e|n|Order; a regular and imposing arrangement; disposition in regular lines; hence, order of battle; as, drawn up in battle array. ; The whole body of persons thus placed in order; an orderly collection; hence, a body of soldiers. ; An imposing series of things. ; Dress; garments disposed in order upon the person; rich or beautiful apparel. ; A ranking or setting forth in order, by the proper officer, of a jury as impaneled in a cause. ; The panel itself. ; The whole body of jurors summoned to attend the court. ; To place or dispose in order, as troops for battle; to marshal. ; To deck or dress; to adorn with dress; to cloth to envelop; -- applied esp. to dress of a splendid kind. ; To set in order, as a jury, for the trial of a cause; that is, to call them man by man.	a:278q,127,4;njk,125,3;1hrw,108,61;1fne,89,3;1hnl,75,5;lyu,75,11;9d4,74,5;2eax,69,14;2gj6,69,20;ngf,67,6;q2z,51,5;1dkl,48,1;a3w,39,4;18y3,37,14;11t2,34,4~1hrw,108,61;2gj6,69,20;2eax,69,14;18y3,37,14;lyu,75,11;ngf,67,6;q2z,51,5;9d4,74,5;2ghj,24,5;1hnl,75,5;278q,127,4;a3w,39,4;11t2,34,4;158d,19,4;njk,125,3	v:2020,3,3~2020,3,3	V:gjk,49,4;u98,44,2;gjm,31,3;1r8m,11,1;2e5h,8,1;b50,2,1~gjk,49,4;gjm,31,3;u98,44,2;2e5h,8,1;b50,2,1;1r8m,11,1	n:24z7,63,9;1dkl,58,2;1gfj,54,8;13f3,49,7;1voz,42,3;243a,9,3;2020,3,3;1hqk,3,3~24z7,63,9;1gfj,54,8;13f3,49,7;2020,3,3;243a,9,3;1voz,42,3;1hqk,3,3;1dkl,58,2	N:1veu,43,3;pjb,40,2;21cl,27,5;gjm,15,1;2e5h,8,1~21cl,27,5;1veu,43,3;pjb,40,2;gjm,15,1;2e5h,8,1
